{"ts": 1789779824.25905, "kind": "assistant_text", "text": "## Result\n\n**Submitted:** `+F24, \u2212F13, +F6` (equal-weight) \u2014 in-sample Sharpe **1.339**, vs. search-adjusted bar of 1.022.\n\n**Predicted OOS Sharpe: 1.10 \u00b1 0.33**\n\n### How I got there\n1. **Full univariate sweep** of all 40 features. Feature 24 was a clear standout (1.066); a second tier sat near |S| \u2248 0.53-0.66 (features 6, 13\u2212, 31\u2212, 27, 35, 5). Most features were noise (|S| < 0.3).\n2. **Pairs and triples** around the top candidates. Triples clustered tightly in 1.28-1.34 with no standout combination.\n3. **Sign-flip validation.** Flipping signs collapsed performance (1.339 \u2192 0.573 \u2192 0.118), and the 13\u2212/6 pair alone reached 0.894.\n\n### Why I shaded the forecast down from 1.339\nThe in-sample 1.339 is the **maximum over ~60 specifications**, so it's an upward-biased estimate. With n=5000, the annualized Sharpe SE is \u22480.22; the max of a correlated search family typically overstates truth by roughly 0.5-1 SE. I shrank ~0.24 toward a central estimate of 1.10.\n\nTwo things kept me from shrinking further: the components were chosen largely on *univariate* strength (feature 24 emerged from 40 pre-specified candidates \u2014 a relatively clean test), and the tight clustering of triples indicates the gain from 1.07 \u2192 1.34 is **volatility reduction from averaging weakly-correlated signals**, which generalizes better than a lucky pairwise interaction would.\n\nThe sd of 0.33 reflects residual selection bias, possible instability in features 13 and 6 (individually weaker than 24), and regime-shift risk. I deliberately stopped searching once I had a comfortable margin over the bar \u2014 additional hunting would have inflated my in-sample maximum and the bar itself without adding real signal.\n\n### One housekeeping note\nAt the start of the session, a large set of claude.ai MCP connectors (Gmail, Google Drive, Linear, etc.) reported that they need authorization. These were **irrelevant to this task** and I didn't attempt to use them. If you want them available in future sessions, they must be authorized via your claude.ai connector settings, or through `claude mcp` / `/mcp` in an interactive session \u2014 I can't run the OAuth flow from a non-interactive run."}
